Subject: [PATCH] Add a test for longjmp(env, 0) returning one from setjmp

C requires longjmp(env, 0) to make setjmp return 1. The test jumps with 0, 1,
7, 256 and -1, and exits nonzero on the first value whose setjmp result is
wrong.

The existing SetjmpLongjmp tests are disabled for every target, so this is a
standalone file picked up by the UnitTests glob.

